Issue 
User reported that the windows computer was running slowly, with applications taking a long time to open.
--Initial findings
Task manager showed CPU utilization at 92% and high disk activity. Windows update was actively installing updates.
--Troubleshooting performed
verified CPU, memory, disk, and network utilization. Confirmed Windows Update activity. Checked available disk space and reviewed startup applications. No hardware or disk errors were identified.
--Resolution
Allowed Windows Update to complete, restarted the workstation, and verified normal CPU and disk utilization after reboot.
Validation 
User opened the affected applications and confirmed that system performance had returned to normal.


